// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row rcdyn_borrow_arg_no_vtable (tier 4, `diag`). An ILLEGAL program is refused with a BACKEND internal error:
// passing `&r` for a `&dyn Sp` parameter, where `r` is an `Rc<dyn Sp>` local, fails in mlir-gen with
//
//   mlir_gen: internal: no vtable for 'Rc$G1$udyn_Sp' as '&dyn Sp' — the fat pointer's vtable half would be left uninitialised …
//
// compile rc 1, no object file, no `error:` line.
//
// RECLASSIFIED 2026-09-15f-rustcaudit from tier 3 `refuses`: the row said "legal — `&Rc<dyn Sp>` deref-coerces to `&dyn Sp`", a READING.
// legality: rustc 1.98.1 --edition 2024 on the twin src/compiler/probes/2026-09-15f-rustcaudit/rust/rcdyn_borrow_arg_no_vtable.rs: REFUSED
//   error[E0277]: the trait bound `Rc<dyn Sp>: Sp` is not satisfied — "required for the cast from `&Rc<dyn Sp>` to `&dyn Sp`"
// The verdict is right; the sentence is the defect (E0277). The legal spelling `use_ref(&*r)` compiles and runs 0 on the same binary
// (twin src/compiler/probes/2026-09-15f-rustcaudit/rust/control/tier34/rcdyn_explicit_deref.rs, exit 0), so no legal-refusal defect remains on this construct.
// The old row's one-token control (`Box` for `Rc`, tests/logos/pass/boxdyn_borrow_arg_keeps_box_drop) is ALSO E0277 in rustc — reported for the owner.
package rcdyn_borrow_arg_no_vtable;
use logos.lang.rc;

trait Sp { fn v(&self) -> i64; }
struct A { x: i64 }
impl Sp for A { fn v(&self) -> i64 { return self.x; } }

fn use_ref(r: &dyn Sp) -> i64 { return r.v(); }

fn main() -> i32 {
    let r: Rc<dyn Sp> = rc_new(A { x: 42i64 });
    if use_ref(&r) != 42i64 { return 3i32; }
    return 0i32;
}
